      "id": "yeats-collected-poems-s0224-p00466",
      "source_en": "Must we part, Von Hugel, though much alike, for we\nAccept the miracles of the saints and honour sanctity?\n The· body of Saint Teresa lies undecayed in tomb, 8o\nBathed in miraculous oil, sweet odours from it come,\nHealing from its lettered slab. Those self-same hands\nperchance\nEternalised the body of a modern saint that once\nHad scooped out Pharaoh's mummy. I - though heart might\nfind relief\nDid I become a Christian man and choose for my belief\nWhat seems most welcome in the tomb - play a predestined\npart.",
